<title>ITALY: Deroma makes Milan debut at 11,950 lire.</title>
<headline>Deroma makes Milan debut at 11,950 lire.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian terracotta pot maker Deroma Holding finally made its Milan stock market debut at 11,950 lire against a share placement price of 10,000 lire, but slipped back by midsession.</p>
<p>At 1155 GMT, the stock was quoted at 11,570 lire bid/11,580 ask in volume of over 730,000 shares.</p>
<p>The share was suspended early on when it went limit up but managed to be quoted when the 10 percent trading limit was widened to 20 percent.</p>
<p>The Vicenza-based group, a world leader in its field, floated 5.6 million shares deriving from a capital increase.</p>
<p>It had estimated 1996 turnover of 114 billion lire with some 80 percent coming from sales abroad.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
